%% Castling — two-phase move on the physical board game_task.c
%%{init: {'theme':'dark','themeVariables':{'fontFamily':'system-ui,sans-serif','clusterBkg':'#0f172a','clusterBorder':'#334155','lineColor':'#94a3b8','primaryTextColor':'#f1f5f9','edgeLabelBackground':'#1e293b','titleColor':'#f8fafc'}}}%%
flowchart TD
  A[King move by 2 squares e→g / e→c] --> B[game_validate_castling — king/rook · empty path · king not in check · path squares not attacked]
  B -->|error| E[MOVE_ERROR_CASTLING_BLOCKED …]
  B -->|OK| C[game_execute_move → MOVE_TYPE_CASTLE_*]

  C --> D[game_execute_move_enhanced: moves only KING · rook STAYS on a/h]
  D --> F[castling_state.in_progress = true · rook_from/to · LED guide]
  F --> G[Player does NOT switch — waiting for second rook move]

  G --> H[Next move: game_is_valid_move]
  H --> I{Exactly rook move rook_from → rook_to?}
  I -->|yes| J[Validation exception — skip rook geometry · check test]
  I -->|king elsewhere| K[Possible castling cancel — castling_state = false see code]
  I -->|else| L[Waiting / error]

  J --> M[game_execute_move finish: write rook to board · in_progress = false · king/rook moved flags]
  M --> N[Switch player · timers · highlight / check animation]
